title ALES41 — Lotus's two-band tone shelf: bass and treble from the one-pole split
prompt Continue the ALES recursion loop Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds and make progress before checking in; send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur
think ALES40 landed the one-pole low-pass and its exact high-pass complement, but a filter alone only REMOVES a band. The tone control a keeper actually turns is two knobs — bass and treble — each boosting OR cutting its band. ALES40 already gives the split whose sum reconstructs the input (low_pass + high_pass = x), so a two-band shelf is that split with each band scaled and summed — the everyday equalizer. Chosen Lindy-first (bass/treble are the two controls on every amp and mixer ever shipped) crux-first (the hard-but-tractable core is ALES8's fader lesson — scale in the wide domain, clamp once).
think Shape: lotus/shelf.rye over tone + timeline. The low band lives in a scratch Clip copy of the span (so the original samples, the high band's minuend, stay intact until the combine writes them); tone.low_pass runs on the scratch; then per sample L = low[i], x = clip[i], H = x - L, and out = saturate(divTrunc(bass_num*L, bass_den) + divTrunc(treble_num*H, treble_den)) — each band divided in i64, summed in i64, one clamp over the true sum. ShelfError = tone.ToneError || error{BadGain} (the filter's BadCoeff/BadRange reused whole, plus a zero band denominator).
think Two properties make the shelf honest and witnessable. Unity is identity: bass=bass_den, treble=treble_den writes L + (x - L) = x exactly — a flat EQ passes through untouched, the sharpest proof the bands reconstruct. Orthogonal at direct current: a settled constant has H = 0 exactly (ALES40's proven DC removal), so treble cannot move a constant and only bass scales it — a constant at bass 2/1 doubles, the same constant at any treble unchanged. This orthogonality is the clean, exactly-provable claim (bass moves the low end, treble the high end, neither reaches across at DC).
obs GREEN on the first build across six cases: silence stays silence; unity on both bands (1/1, 1/1) at coefficient 1/3 wrote a six-sample input byte-for-byte (identity); a constant 1000 over 30 samples at bass 2/1 treble 1/1 settled its tail to exactly 2000 with the first sample still in transient; the same constant at bass 1/1 treble 5/1 left the settled tail exactly 1000 (treble cannot touch DC); a loud 20000 constant at bass 2/1 SATURATED to +32767 rather than wrapping; a zero and an above-one coefficient each refused BadCoeff, a zero bass and a zero treble denominator each refused BadGain, an out-of-range span refused BadRange leaving the clip untouched.
obs Witness tools/ales_shelf_witness.rish GREEN; tame_style_check GREEN (bans clean). Reused whole: tone.low_pass, tone.ToneError, timeline.Clip/saturate/splice. The scratch Clip is one stack copy (max_clip 4096 samples = 8 KB), local to the call. Purely local — bounded i16 PCM; no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no real sample rate (the coefficient sets the split over sample indices, not a crossover in hertz — a real time base is a later rung); every custody gate untouched.
loom witness=ales_shelf_witness result=green build=first cases=6 bands=2 domain=i64-wide clamp=single reused=tone.low_pass+timeline.saturate
file lotus/shelf.rye ALES41 module — a two-band tone shelf scaling ALES40's low and high bands independently and clamping once, unity the identity and a boost saturating
file tools/ales_shelf_witness.rish the witness that builds and proves it GREEN on metal
file active-designing/20260814-161231_fill-ales41-lotus-tone-shelf.md the self-approved design read for the round
file lotus/README.md front door synced — status list (ALES41 tone shelf), the shelf.rye rung entry, road-on paragraph
recommend keep-going ALES42 can add a mid band (a third knob from a band-pass of the two poles), carry the filter state across a re-berthed span so a shelf spans without a fresh transient, or name the crossover in hertz through a real time base; the signed and wire session carries stay module seams for Keaton's word
